t is reasonable to do the same here.\r\n\r\nI suspect that using jasmine's [mock clock][2] would be a better solution for such cases :smiley:\r\n\r\n[1]: https://github.com/angular/angular/pull/19904/files#diff-664eb094568ce031b715e2b114d6166cR275\r\n[2]: https://jasmine.github.io/api/2.8/Clock.html","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/353177230/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"gkalpak","id":8604205,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2MDQyMDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8604205?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak","html_url":"https://github.com/gkalpak","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gkalpak/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/353607690","html_url":"https://github.com/angular/angular/issues/21112#issuecomment-353607690","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/21112","id":353607690,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM1MzYwNzY5MA==","user":{"login":"teh-skrud","id":5594717,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1OTQ3MTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5594717?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/teh-skrud","html_url":"https://github.com/teh-skrud","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teh-skrud/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teh-skrud/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teh-skrud/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teh-skrud/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teh-skrud/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teh-skrud/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teh-skrud/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teh-skrud/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/teh-skrud/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-12-22T14:24:38Z","updated_at":"2017-12-22T15:21:12Z","body":"I don't think that Jasmine.clock() can be useful here as it only mocks calls to `new Date()` (i.e. it is used to mock \"now\"), but we are using `new Date(ISOString)`.\r\n\r\nHowever, why not simply passing an ISOString including a timezone to it ? (i.e. '2017-05-07T22:14:39+0000') \r\nFrom my understanding, that would still be a valid test to prevent regression for the #9524 bug (@ocombe ?).\r\n\r\nEDIT : actually, it doesn't matter as the datePipe outputs a formatted date in the local TZ (it uses Date.prototype.getHours() and similar methods which all are local time dependents). So passing a TZ in the ISOString is of no value (cf the failed test referenced in this issue). So yeah, maybe using 12:00 is the least worst way of solving this.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/353607690/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"teh-skrud","id":5594717,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU1OTQ3MTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.gith